# @videoskillet/videoskillet

A real-time NTSC signal path in WebGPU compute shaders — the engine behind
[videoskillet.com](https://videoskillet.com/).

`Engine.create` takes a canvas and runs the pass graph on it: RGB is encoded to
a composite waveform, the waveform is impaired, and a simulated receiver decodes
what is left. The artifacts come out of the mechanism, so dot crawl, ringing,
head switching noise and sync loss interact the way the analog ones do.

```ts
import { Engine } from '@videoskillet/videoskillet'

const engine = await Engine.create(canvas)
engine.setControl('noiseIre', 4)
engine.setControl('rfSnow', 0.3)
engine.step()
```

The signal-domain modules under `core/signal/` are plain TypeScript with no GPU
dependency. A host can drive the fault, glide and stability planners on its own.

## Requirements

A WebGPU context. The engine presents to an `HTMLCanvasElement` or an
`OffscreenCanvas`, and the audio return path wants Web Audio where it is
available.

